H1: Prop Firm CRM API & Trading Technology
Running a prop firm looks simple from the outside. Sell a challenge, give the trader an account, check whether they pass. In reality, the operations behind it get complicated fast. Hundreds or thousands of evaluation accounts, each with its own phase, rules and deadlines. Breaches that need to be caught as they happen. Payouts that need checking before money goes out. Affiliates, discount codes, certificates, support tickets.
A prop firm CRM built for that model brings it all into one system, connected to your trading platform through an API, so your team can manage traders at scale without living in spreadsheets.
CTA: Discuss Prop Firm Technology
H2: Why Prop Firms Need Their Own CRM
A standard brokerage CRM is designed around deposits, withdrawals and ongoing trading accounts. A prop firm works differently. Traders buy a challenge rather than funding an account. They move through evaluation phases with specific rules. Accounts get created, monitored, breached, reset or promoted, often automatically. Payouts are based on performance on a funded account, not on withdrawing a client's own money.
Trying to run that on a brokerage CRM, or on a general sales tool, usually means a lot of manual work and a lot of room for mistakes. Prop firm CRM software is built around the challenge lifecycle from the start, which is why it handles the volume and the rules properly.
H2: The Prop Firm Workflow, Covered End to End
H3: Challenge Sales and Checkout
 Traders choose a challenge, by account size, phase structure or rule set, and pay through integrated payment providers. Discount codes, promotions and affiliate referrals are applied at checkout and tracked automatically.
H3: Trader Onboarding
 Once payment clears, the trader's profile is created in the CRM and their evaluation account is set up on the trading platform through the API, with the correct balance, leverage and group for their challenge. Login details are sent automatically.
H3: Rule Monitoring
 Each challenge has its own rules: profit targets, daily loss limits, maximum drawdown, minimum trading days, time limits and any restrictions you set. The system tracks trading activity against those rules and flags breaches or completed targets as they happen.
H3: Phase Progression
 When a trader passes a phase, they can be moved to the next one automatically or after review. New accounts are created, old ones closed, and the trader is notified.
H3: Funded Accounts
 Traders who pass the evaluation move to a funded or simulated funded account, depending on your model, with the rules and profit split that apply at that stage.
H3: Payout Requests
 Funded traders request payouts through their dashboard. Requests move through a review workflow where your team checks trading activity, rule compliance and verification status before approving.
H3: KYC
 Identity verification can be required at the point you choose, often before a funded account is issued or before the first payout. Documents and verification results are stored in the trader's profile.
H3: Resets and Retakes
 Traders who breach a rule can be offered a reset or a new challenge at the price you set, handled through the same checkout and account creation flow.
H2: Key Features
H3: Trader Dashboard
 A branded area where traders see their challenges, account status, progress against targets, rule limits, trading statistics and payout history. Clear dashboards cut down on support questions like "why was my account breached?" because traders can see it themselves.
H3: Challenge and Rule Configuration
 Set up multiple challenge types with different account sizes, phase structures, targets, loss limits, drawdown types and time rules. Changes to your offer don't need a developer.
H3: Automated Account Management
 Evaluation and funded accounts are created, updated, disabled or closed automatically through the platform API, based on purchases, rule outcomes and phase changes.
H3: Breach and Pass Detection
 Rules are checked against trading activity so breaches and passes are identified quickly and consistently, with clear records showing what happened and when.
H3: Payout Management
 Payout requests, reviews, approvals and history in one place, with checks built in before anything is paid.
H3: Affiliate Management
 Track affiliates, their referred traders and their commissions, with their own portal access for statistics and earnings.
H3: Discount Codes and Promotions
 Create and track codes, campaigns and seasonal offers, and see which ones actually drive sales.
H3: Certificates
 Generate certificates automatically when traders pass a phase or receive a payout, ready to share. Many traders post these publicly, which doubles as marketing.
H3: Support and Communication
 Automated emails for purchases, account credentials, breaches, passes and payouts, plus a record of every communication in the trader's profile.
H3: Reporting
 Sales, pass rates, breach patterns, payout totals, affiliate performance and revenue by challenge type, giving you a clear view of how the business is performing.
H3: Role-Based Access
 Different access for support, risk, finance and management, with a record of actions taken.
H2: The Prop Firm API
The API is what connects the CRM to your trading platform and to anything else you want to plug in.
On the platform side, it handles account creation, configuration, monitoring and status changes, along with pulling the trading data needed for rule checks, dashboards and reporting.
On the business side, a prop firm API also lets you connect your own website, checkout, marketing tools, analytics or internal systems. If you have developers, they can build custom features on top of the CRM rather than working around it.
Which trading platform you connect to depends on your setup and the platform arrangements available to you. Platform availability for prop firms can depend on provider terms, so we'll confirm what's realistic for your business during planning rather than assuming.
H2: Risk and Payout Controls
The integrity of a prop firm depends on its rules being applied consistently and its payouts being checked properly.
The system records every rule check and outcome, so decisions can be explained if a trader questions them. Payout workflows can include checks on trading behaviour, verification status and rule compliance before approval. Your risk team gets visibility into patterns, such as the same trader running several accounts or unusual activity around news events, so they can investigate.
The policies themselves are your decisions. The technology makes sure they're applied fairly and traceably.
